  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\n[The spec just says](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/canvas.html#drawing-model):\n\n> Composite B within the [clipping region](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/canvas.html#clipping-region) over the current [output bitmap](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/canvas.html#output-bitmap) using the [current compositing and blending operator](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/canvas.html#current-compositing-and-blending-operator).\n\nWhich I understood as non-isolated blending, but it's actually isolated blending (per WPT tests). It would be nice to state that explicitly, as currently browsers are not respecting this (Firefox vs Edge):\n\n![](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/90a77625-8d18-4416-8f58-c87aede24634)",
